{"id":"0b69e342-f385-4663-b1dd-79f5a99f1ab4","object":"chat.completion","created":1785030978,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    nodes = case[\\\"nodes\\\"]\\n    required_symbols = set(case[\\\"required_symbols\\\"])\\n    node_by_id = {n[\\\"id\\\"]: n for n in nodes}\\n    children = {n[\\\"id\\\"]: [] for n in nodes}\\n    for n in nodes:\\n        p = n.get(\\\"parent\\\")\\n        if p:\\n            children[p].append(n[\\\"id\\\"])\\n    retained = {n[\\\"id\\\"] for n in nodes}\\n    removed = []\\n    sorted_nodes = sorted(nodes, key=lambda n: (-n[\\\"depth\\\"], n[\\\"id\\\"]))\\n    for node in sorted_nodes:\\n        nid = node[\\\"id\\\"]\\n        if nid not in retained:\\n            continue\\n        if not node[\\\"removable\\\"]:\\n            continue\\n        if node[\\\"parent\\\"] is None:\\n            continue\\n        if node[\\\"symbol\\\"] in required_symbols:\\n            continue\\n        if any(cid in retained for cid in children.get(nid, [])):\\n            continue\\n        syms = set()\\n        for rid in retained:\\n            if rid == nid:\\n                continue\\n            syms.add(node_by_id[rid][\\\"symbol\\\"])\\n        if not required_symbols.issubset(syms):\\n            continue\\n        retained.remove(nid)\\n        removed.append(nid)\\n    return {\\n        \\\"removed_node_ids\\\": removed,\\n        \\\"retained_node_ids\\\": sorted(retained)\\n    }\"\n}","reasoning_content":"We need to implement solve(case) for task SE-PE-01. The case has a payload with nodes (each with id, parent, symbol, depth, removable, utility) and required_symbols list. The output must have removed_node_ids (list of strings) and retained_node_ids (list of strings). The description: grammar_guided_node_reduction, based on Perses-style reduction. We need to simulate a reduction algorithm that tries to remove removable nodes while preserving required symbols and that the tree remains valid? The description mentions \"grammar-valid deletion and replacement candidates\" but we don't have a grammar. However, we have required_symbols, which are symbols that must remain represented in the tree. So the tree must contain at least one node with each required symbol after removal. Also, we must consider \"deeper before shallower\" (post-order traversal). Tentatively remove a node if all required symbols remain represented. Also, \"never remove the root, a required symbol, or a node with retained children\". So nodes that are not removable (removable=false) cannot be removed. Also, if a node's symbol is in required_symbols, it cannot be removed. Also, if a node has any child that is retained (i.e., not removed), then we cannot remove the node because that would orphan the child? Actually \"never remove a node with retained children\" means if a node has children that are still in the tree, we cannot remove it. That is typical in tree reduction: removing a node means its children become children of the node's parent, but here we are just marking nodes as removed. But the description says \"Tentatively remove a node only if all required symbols remain represented.\" So we need to simulate a removal process.\n\nThe node ID is used as stable tie-breaker at equal depth.\n\nThe output order: removed_node_ids is the actual removal order (the order in which nodes were removed). retained_node_ids are the IDs of nodes that are not removed, and should be sorted? The contract says \"Return sorted retained IDs and the actual removal order.\" So retained_node_ids should be sorted ascending? Typically ascending alphabetical or numerical? In the fixture, node IDs are strings like \"n1\", \"n2\", \"root\". Sorting lexicographically would give \"n1\", \"n2\", \"n3\", ..., \"root\". But \"root\" comes before \"n1\" lexicographically (since 'r' > 'n'? Actually 'r' is greater than 'n', so \"root\" > \"n1\"? Let's ch